cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Laurel corpus: English verse in TEI, with scansion and canonical references"
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dome
    given-names: Garrett
repository-code: "https://github.com/laurel-corpus/laurel-corpus"
# The concept DOI: it always resolves to the newest version of the corpus. The DOI for this release
# alone is 10.5281/zenodo.22738548, which is what to cite when a result depends on exactly these texts.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22738547"
version: v1.0.1
date-released: 2026-09-14
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22738547"
    description: "All versions of the Laurel corpus"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22738548"
    description: "Version 1.0.1"
url: "https://laurelpoetry.com"
abstract: >-
  416 works of public domain English verse encoded in TEI P5: 18,210 poems and
  1,201,722 lines, each line carrying both the stress the words settle and the
  stress its metre asks for. Every poem has a canonical reference naming its
  edition, on the CTS model, and a permanent identifier that survives re-titling.
  1,680 poems carry line-level timings against public domain recordings.
keywords:
  - poetry
  - prosody
  - scansion
  - metre
  - TEI
  - digital humanities
  - public domain
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
